# Per-route 200 rewrites point at "/" (or a locale directory like "/en/"), NOT
# "/index.html": Cloudflare Pages 308-redirects /index.html to its directory,
# and that normalisation applies to rewrite targets too, so "/login /index.html
# 200" sent every deep link home. Rewrite to "/" serves the same file.
# The /* catch-all MUST stay "/index.html": a catch-all rewrite to "/" serves
# the app shell for every static file (JS, images, sw.js) instead of the file.
#
# Exception (2026-11-25, mythic-atlas/social fix): a wildcard rewrite to "/"
# ALSO shadows every static file under that path (verified live 2026-11-25:
# all 109 files under /mythic-atlas/* and /social/* returned the app shell
# instead of the file). So wildcard rewrites for paths that hold static files
# MUST point at "/index.html" (static files win; verified with wrangler pages
# dev), while the bare route keeps "/ 200" — no static file lives at the bare
# path, and "/index.html" there 308-redirects the route home.

